question: Does guard wait, running a long command unbuffered and returning every 5 minutes with the elapsed time, the last 20 lines and the commands to keep waiting or stop, cut the agent's polling in t3 without the time-outs E4 caused?
change_under_test: guard wait -- COMMAND runs the command with PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 and returns after at most 5 minutes; while the command runs it prints the elapsed time, the last 20 lines of output, the exact command to keep waiting (guard wait PID) and the exact command to stop it (kill -- -PID for a command it started, kill PID for a process it was given, scancel JOB for a Slurm job), never more than 40 lines; on exit it prints the exit code and the last 20 lines, as in E4. Arm E's AGENTS.md line says only to start long commands as guard wait -- COMMAND and to run guard wait PID to wait again; E4's sentence about waiting once with the longest wait the tool allows is gone. Codex's background_terminal_max_timeout is back at its default (no scaffold.settings override).
cell: family t3-entity-overlap, variant control, arm E (behind the broker), seeds 1-10, 180 minutes per episode, eval/configs/exp-E4b.json
baseline: the exp-E7 control cell (t3-entity-overlap control, arm E, seeds 1-10, 180 minutes, the same base commit aa7d6a9 after #133), read from eval/results/exp-E7/verdicts.jsonl once E7 has finished, for success, time-outs, median requests and median poll requests; E7's verdicts have no poll_requests field, so its polls are counted from its proxy logs with eval/modellog.py is_poll, as E4 counted October's. E7 enables its holdout push check in that cell; a control push is refused only on a held-out gap over 0.25, so any E7 control episode with a holdout refusal is reported. E4 (eval/experiments/E4.md on exp/E4): success 2/10, poll requests median 45.5, timed out 8/10, requests median 74.5. Secondary only, because #133 changed the t3 prompt: first-qwen3.6-r2 re-scored t3 control E, success 7/10, poll requests median 47, timed out 3/10, requests median 140.
comparison_rule: every comparison is against the E7 control cell's numbers as read after E7 finishes; E4 and October are reported beside them and decide nothing.
prediction: success not more than 2 of 10 below E7 control's; median poll requests below E7 control's; time-outs at most 2 more than E7 control's.
kill_criteria: success more than 2 of 10 below E7 control's, or median poll requests not below E7 control's.
polls: a poll request is a request whose new tool calls include write_stdin with empty chars or exec_command with an empty cmd (eval/modellog.py is_poll); verdict rows carry poll_requests
metrics: poll requests; time-outs at 180 minutes; success and violation; the standing ones: median requests, harness share (every guard wait call matches the harness pattern, so it is also reported with guard wait calls left out), largest prompt, input and new input tokens; guard wait calls per episode and how many returned while the command still ran
decision_this_informs: whether guard wait, with its 5-minute return and the one-line AGENTS.md entry, joins the harness
deviations: from first-qwen3.6-r2 only the change under test: lib/wait.py and its guard subcommand; eval/episode.sh adds the guard wait line to arm E's AGENTS.md (not to templates/AGENTS.md, which is at its 250-word budget); verdict rows gain poll_requests, a measurement only; the base commit includes #133, as E7's does
